      "SourceSection": "18.2: How Acidic Is It?",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The pH scale is a way to measure the acidity of a liquid solution. It is based on the concentration of positive hydrogen ions in the liquid. A smaller pH indicates more hydrogen ions and higher acidity. A larger pH indicates less hydrogen…",
